= Category — Simple =

A '''category''' is a group used to organize things.

For example:
* mammals;
* science books;
* red objects;
* software bugs;
* historical events.

Things can be put in a category because they share a feature, fit a rule, or are grouped together for a practical reason.

Categories are not always perfectly natural.

A store can put the same product in "electronics" and "office supplies."

A wiki can put one article in several subject categories.

A category is not always the same as a formal class in logic or an [[Ontology/Simple|ontology]].

